this video was made possible by class  central.com / Pakman which lets you  watch tens of thousands of lectures from  the world's best universities check it  out by clicking the link underneath this  video this episode of the pseudo-science  mini-series brings us to UFOs  unidentified flying objects and claims  about extraterrestrial life visiting  earth the existence of extraterrestrial  life is a subject of real scientific  inquiry telescopes scan the cosmos for  evidence and radio listening devices  search the galaxy for interstellar  communications well known probability  equations like the Drake Equation  suggest that the existence of  extraterrestrial life is possible and  maybe even probable but the popular and  speculative study of reports surrounding  alien attributed UFOs is called UF ology  and it is pseudoscience ufology  investigation encompasses things like  UFO sightings alien contact and  abduction stories and supposed  government conspiracies and cover-ups of  such things and as in many  pseudo-sciences claims about UFOs and  aliens are rife with unfalsifiable  propositions questionable assumptions  and flimsy or even non-existent evidence  the first modern UFO sighting to gain  widespread news coverage was by private  pilot Kenneth Arnold in 1947 he was  flying over a national park in  Washington State and he says he saw a  number of mysterious objects miles away  from him that looked like Crescent  shapes skipping on water and in response  to Arnold's own detailed descriptions of  what he saw there have been a number of  alternative explanations offered by  experts who have closely examined the  situation including that the objects  might have been mirages or misidentified  meteors or Birds or clouds of snow  nevertheless news reports describing the  sighting gave rise to the term flying  saucer although all Arnold actually said  he had been misquoted by reporters when  they use the word saucer but this common  theme is one that we deal with a lot  with UFO claims it's often just a game  of telephone first-hand accounts are  often sensationalized and in 1949 alone  two  years after Arnold's misreported quote  flying saucer sighting the government  reported 256 UFO sightings roughly 70%  of which were described as something  reminiscent of a flying saucer private  and government inquiry into these  sightings found conclusively that many  of these UFOs were merely misidentified  high-altitude weather balloons many of  which had lights and other electronic  equipment attached to them  meteors bol IDEs and even planets Venus  is actually often mistaken for a UFO  it's the brightest object in the sky  when it's visible and it often appears  near the horizon then in the 1960s there  were a number of UFO sightings in Nevada  that were later attributed to test  flights of highly classified CIA  aircraft like the ox cart and u2 spy  planes in 2009 a spiraling light in the  skies above Norway was reported the  Russian military later explained that it  was a missile that failed to launch  which subsequently spiraled out of  control  in October of 2010 hundreds of people  reported UFOs above New York City's  shiny silvery objects in the sky turns  out somebody accidentally released 12  helium balloons at a party in  Westchester County which then drifted  over to New York City there's a long  list of UFO sightings throughout the  20th century that were debunked by  documents Declassified by the CIA in  2007 those documents are definitely  worth checking out one of the first  famous accounts of alien abduction was  by New Hampshire couple Betty and Barney  Hill in 1961 who said they had been  kidnapped by extraterrestrials from the  Zeta Reticuli system Barney Hill  revealed details about the aliens who  supposedly abducted him and his wife and  historians have noted that Hills  descriptions of the aliens and the  entire situation actually were  strikingly similar to an episode of the  TV show Outer Limits which had aired  just two weeks before Hill gave the  account in 1964 he'll describe the  aliens behavior their physical  appearance and their clothing all of  which matched the Outer Limits episode  that recently aired Betty Hills account  of the incident also was curious  similar to other previous alien fiction  before they were abducted Betty read  Donald Kehoe's book the flying saucer  conspiracy which depicts four dwarf like  creatures appearing out of a hovering  object and eventually dragging two  people into their ship to examine them  this story closely resembles Betty Hills  account of what happened we also know  that before the supposed abduction Betty  Hill was already abnormally interested  in UFOs like I said she read the Flying  Saucer conspiracy before the supposed  abduction and she even wrote letters to  the author  Betty Hills sister also claims to have  seen a UFO years before Betty and  Barney's incident many people who have  reported alien abduction have later been  determined to have actually been  experiencing what's known as sleep  paralysis which is a real medical  phenomenon it can include hallucinations  of flashing lights buzzing sounds  experiences of floating even impressions  of  other people being in the room and a  2002 Harvard study entitled memory  distortion in people reporting abduction  by aliens found that people who claimed  abductions are also prone to what's  called false memory syndrome when given  memory tests alien abductees regularly  claim to recall words items and  sentences that they hadn't actually seen  false memories and sleep paralysis  definitely seem like more convincing  explanations for accounts like these as  opposed to actual alien abduction by  extraterrestrials but most importantly  abduction claims have no concrete  evidence and have relied only on the  accounts of those involved and nothing  else many UFO lodges claim that the US  government is involved in cover-ups of  UFO and alien abduction incidents  according to declassified memos when UFO  sightings became more widespread after  World War two  the CIA did conceal its investigation of  these sightings from public view for  fear of inflaming quote alarmist  tendencies but this is very different  from covering up the existence of actual  aliens area 51 a highly secretive Air  Force Base in Nevada has been the  subject of a lot of speculation by UF  ologists but  area 51 secrecy isn't proof of anything  tight security at area 51 and other  similar military installations make  sense given that highly classified  aircraft are developed and tested at  these sites one of the most  sensationalized events in UFO folklore  is the famous Roswell incident when in  July of 1947 just outside Roswell New  Mexico an unidentified object crashed to  the ground inside a sheep pasture one of  the men who found the crashed object  described that it was made partly of a  strange indestructible metallic foil  material he had never seen or heard of  before an Air Force Base recovered the  wreckage and a Roswell newspaper ran a  story claiming that a flying saucer had  crashed the next day an air force  official stated it was actually just a  conventional weather balloon but  photographs of the wreckage made it  clear that the object was far too large  and technologically equipped to be a  weather balloon and for decades UF  ologist developed complex conspiracy  theories about the object in Roswell  being of extraterrestrial origin and the  government's efforts to cover it up  several pieces of footage surfaced that  showed autopsies performed on the aliens  found at the crash but the filmmakers  later admitted that they were just  hoaxes in 1994 and 1997 the US military  released two reports revealing that the  crashed object was one of many highly  classified nuclear surveillance balloons  deside designed to monitor nuclear  testing by the Soviet Union which would  very reasonably explain why the  government would want to keep them  secret the CIA and Air Force have long  investigated the legitimacy of UFO  reports with various teams of scientists  and military experts last major  government investigation was called  Project Blue Book which took place from  1952 to 1970 the summary of the findings  were clear stating quote there is no  evidence submitted to or discovered by  the Air Force that sightings categorized  as unidentified represent technological  developments or principles beyond the  range of modern scientific  and there was no evidence indicating  that sightings categorized as  unidentified were extraterrestrial  vehicles it's possible and maybe even  mathematically probable that intelligent  life exists somewhere elsewhere in the  universe  however conclusions that aliens have  visited our planet only to be observed  as UFOs or have abducted humans and that  it has all been covered up by government  conspiracy lack actual evidence the  evidence that UFO gist offer is mostly  limited to people's memories alone or  sometimes includes grainy Loch Ness  monster esque photographs Occam's razor  tells us that the simplest solution to a  problem is preferable to a more complex  one if it explains the circumstances  equally well there are a large range of  possible explanations for UFO sightings  and suppose it abductions the least  obvious answer to any of them is aliens  the burden of proof is on the UF  ologists and so far what they've  provided just doesn't hold up but a  great way to find out more about the  real scientific quest for knowledge  about the cosmos and the existence of  aliens is to head over to class  central.com slash Pakman they have an  excellent new course from the University  of Edinburgh called astrobiology and the  search for extraterrestrial life class  central offers tens of thousands of  University courses on almost any topic  you can imagine click the link in the  description to start searching for  top-rated College lectures from  world-renowned universities they've got  